1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:07,775
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, the Spieker Circle is the inscribed circle of the medial triangle M a M b M c.

2
00:00:07,775 --> 00:00:17,850
Named after nineteenth-century geometer Theodor Spieker, its center is the Spieker Center X ten, and its radius is r over two, half the inradius of triangle A B C.

3
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:34,160
Because the medial triangle is the complement of triangle A B C under homothety at the Centroid X two, the Spieker circle is the exact complement of the incircle, and X ten lies on the Nagel line halfway between the Incenter X one and the Nagel Point X eight.

4
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:45,460
Moreover, the Spieker Center X ten is the radical center of the three excircles of triangle A B C, and the Spieker circle is orthogonal to all three excircles in key radical projections.
